cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CLIFForge or its synthetic datasets, please cite it as below."
title: "CLIFForge: A fully synthetic CLIF dataset generator"
abstract: >-
  CLIFForge generates fully synthetic, openly redistributable datasets in the
  Common Longitudinal ICU data Format (CLIF). It uses an empirical-fidelity
  fit-then-sample method: aggregate, non-derivable statistics are fit once from
  real CLIF data, and datasets are then sampled offline from a versioned
  parameter pack so that no real record leaves the fit stage and no synthetic
  record traces back to a real patient. Output conforms exactly to CLIF 2.1 and
  is intended for ETL testing, CI fixtures, teaching, benchmarking, and model
  development where a credentialed real dataset cannot be shared.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rojas
    given-names: J. C.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-26
